<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch03-linear-functions-matrices" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Linear Functions, Linear Transformations, and Matrices</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Linear functions and matrices describe transformations through their action on basis vectors. We study composition, determinants, linear systems, and quadratic forms using the vector algebra already developed. Exact polynomial expansions then introduce the idea of a best linear approximation, preparing for the systematic derivative in Chapter 7.</p>
  </introduction>

